/target
# Cargo.lock IS committed: rustain is a binary/end-product, so the lockfile must be
# version-controlled for reproducible CI. Without it, CI re-resolved deps on every run
# (no --locked) and a newer ratatui patch broke compilation on a fresh resolve while
# local builds stayed green on the cached/old versions (Epic 12 retro follow-up).
*.swp
*.swo
.env
.env.local
*.nu
.claude
.rustain
.rustain_data

# python e2e tui tests
__pycache__
.opencode
graphify-out
AGENTS.md